@@ -15,3 +15,24 @@ language.

 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Authentication and roles
+
+Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, matched against `apiKeys`
+in the data file. Missing, malformed or unknown credentials return 401 with
+code `unauthorized`; insufficient permission returns 403 with code `forbidden`.
+Both use the error shape above.
+
+Viewers can GET all routes except `/audit`. Cooks can also POST to
+`/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures` and
+`/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Managers can use every route.
+The seed keys are `seed-viewer`, `seed-cook` and `seed-manager`.
+
+## Routes
+
+See the Routes list in `README.md` for the existing kitchen endpoints.
+`GET /audit` returns an array of audit entries, newest first, for managers only.
+Each successful write request saves one entry with `time` (ISO instant),
+`keyName`, `method`, `path` (including query string), and response `status`.
+The entry is persisted in the same save as the data change; reads and rejected
+requests do not create entries. Keys and request bodies are never logged.
